# Checks: which error a line keeps when what's in brackets fails (issue #79). Where no words may go ('%~objects%'),
# Skript throws away what parsing the brackets logged; a literal with its type given names a type that isn't one.

function bracketed_errors():
	set {_t} to "x"
	set {_i::*} to indices of ({_t} transformed using [input, input])
	set {_i::*} to indices of (recursive {_t})
	set {_i::*} to indices of (5)
	set {_i::*} to {_t} transformed using [input]
	set {_i::*} to ({_t} transformed using [input])
	set {_i::*} to stone (not a type)
	set {_i::*} to indices of (the 5)
